  Novelty is REAL but INCREMENTAL (novelty_killer): the axis (per-image fixed-ViT latency, budget-invisible) is verifiably distinct from PR#8425 (chunk-boundary correctness) and Sarathi-Serve (text-only). No >=2-source fatal collision exists. But the qualitative headline ("stall-free broken for multimodal") overstates — Sarathi-Serve never gave that guarantee for multimodal. ModServe (2502.00937, uncited) and the encoder-disaggregation production trend bound the impact framing.

  VERDICT: YELLOW — the mechanism is real, the anti-circular control is clean, and the regime-bounded disclosure is scientifically honest. But the claim CANNOT advance to GREEN without the L1 measuring real r (with CUDA Graphs state documented), testing encoder batching behavior, reporting both metrics with CIs, and sweeping production B. The writeup must reframe: not "guarantee broken" but "guarantee never extended to multimodal — here is the quantified gap in worst-iteration stall at small-T regimes." Must cite and contrast with PR#8425 (correctness axis vs latency axis), Sarathi-Serve (text-only scope), and ModServe (encoder disaggregation alternative).

